What are the FUNCTIONS in SQL?
A built-in SQL code that accepts an input value, processes it, and returns an output value

SQL FUNCTIONS TYPES:
1- Single-Row functions - Row-level calculations (one input -> one output) -> more related to preparing data (data engineer)
	* String Functions
	* Numeric Functions
	* Date & Time Functions
	* Null Functions

2- Multi-Row Functions - Aggregations (multiple inputs -> one output) -> more for analysis (data analysts)
	* Aggregate Functions (basics)
	* Window Functions (advanced
